<!-- SECTION 3: WHAT IS GSTAT APPEAL FILING -->
<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">Company Name Change: Legal Process Under Section 13</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>Name change alters Clause I of MOA, requires ROC approval (representing Central Government), and results in fresh COI (INC-25). Effective only after fresh COI issued - company must NOT use new name before this date.</p><p>A name change does NOT create a new entity. CIN, PAN, TAN, all rights, obligations, contracts, assets, liabilities continue. All legal proceedings and agreements continue under the new name. But all registrations must be updated post-COI.</p><p>Post-change updates: PAN card, GST certificate, bank accounts, statutory registers, company seal, letterheads, signage. Patron coordinates everything for Delhi companies.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Change in Name of Company in Delhi:</strong></p>
                    <p><strong>RUN:</strong> Reserve Unique Name. Rs 1,000. 1 proposed + 1 alternative. Reserved 20 days. Trademark pre-check essential.</p><p><strong>Special Resolution:</strong> 75% majority at EGM. Higher threshold than OR for capital changes.</p><p><strong>MGT-14:</strong> Special Resolution filing + linked e-MOA (INC-33) + e-AOA (INC-34). Within 30 days.</p><p><strong>INC-24/INC-25:</strong> Name change application → ROC issues fresh COI with new name, same CIN.</p>

                </div>
            </div>
